{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Darling Corey / Dig a Hole in the Meadow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Dig a hole, dig a hole in the meadow
[D]Dig a hole in the cold, cold ground
[D]Dig a hole, dig a hole in the meadow
[D]Gonna lay [A]darlin Corey [D]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Wake up, wake up darlin Corey
[D]Tell me what makes you sleep so sound
[D]The revenue officers are comin
[D]Gonna tear your [A]still house [D]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Go away, go away darlin Corey
Quit hanging around my bed
That liquor has ruin my body
Pretty women have gone to my head
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh the first time I saw darlin Corey
She was standin in the door
She had her shoes and her stockings in her hand
And her little bare feet on the floor
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh the next time I saw darlin Corey
She was standin by the banks of the sea
she had a 44 strapped around her bosom
And a banjo on her knee
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh the last time I saw darlin Corey
She had a wine glass in her hand
She was drinkin that sweet liquor
With a low down gamblin man.
{end_of_chorus}
